{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39499474",
      "title": "Acting on Mutation Success & Invalidating Queries",
      "sourceHash": "3abd445d8d50c3eecafe393679be8cd445c19a1c83fd78a0f0387782527bbcc8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 1.77,
          "en": "So at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.77,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "whenever we create a new event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "nothing happens because as I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 9.24,
          "en": "at the end of the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.24,
          "end": 11.97,
          "en": "we don't have any code that would define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.97,
          "end": 14.493,
          "en": "what should happen after we mutate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 19.74,
          "en": "Now we could navigate away programmatically, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.74,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "with help of the UseNavigate hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 24.18,
          "en": "provided by React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.18,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "Here in Handle Submit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "we could call Navigate and go back to slash events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "for example, to go back to the starting page essentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "we could do that here, but we also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "might want to wait for this mutation to be finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "until we do that so that we don't close this screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "whilst the request is still on its way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "And we could achieve that by adding another property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "to this useMutation configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "the on success property, which in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "wants a function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.41,
          "end": 67.62,
          "en": "So which is a method that should be added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.62,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "a function that will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 71.943,
          "en": "once this mutation succeeded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.81,
          "end": 77.34,
          "en": "This also makes sure that this code will only execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 79.95,
          "en": "if the mutation did succeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 83.94,
          "en": "If we instead would navigate away here in handleSubmit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.94,
          "end": 85.83,
          "en": "we would always do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.83,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "no matter if the mutation succeeds or fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "So if it fails and an error message should be displayed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 97.443,
          "en": "we would never see that because we instantly navigate away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.06,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "If we instead do that in on success,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "we'll stay on this screen until the mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 106.62,
          "en": "did really succeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.62,
          "end": 109.38300000000001,
          "en": "So any errors would be shown to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "And therefore it's now in here where I want to call Navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 115.68299999999999,
          "en": "and go to slash events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.91,
          "end": 119.7,
          "en": "But that's actually not all I want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 121.83,
          "en": "Instead, if you would go back here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.83,
          "end": 124.44,
          "en": "and you would submit such a new event here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.44,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "by clicking Create, you would see that it is submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "but it's not showing up here under my recently added events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 136.083,
          "en": "which right now are basically all events I have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "It's not showing up here until I, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "switch to a different page and come back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "because as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 148.02,
          "en": "this triggers React Query to refetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.02,
          "end": 149.79,
          "en": "behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.79,
          "end": 153.159,
          "en": "But of course, if I know that the data just changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.159,
          "end": 156.055,
          "en": "because I added a new event, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.055,
          "end": 161.055,
          "en": "I want React Query to immediately refetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 165.498,
          "en": "I wanted to immediately update my data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.498,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "put in other words, here in this new events section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "for this Query, which is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "for fetching those events here, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 180.27,
          "en": "that the data that was fetched here is marked as stale",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.27,
          "end": 183.21,
          "en": "and a refetch is triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "And we can achieve this by calling a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "that's provided by React Query",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 194.69,
          "en": "that allows us to invalidate one or more queries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.54,
          "end": 199.05,
          "en": "So that allows us to tell React Query",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 203.73,
          "en": "that the data that's connected to some queries is outdated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.73,
          "end": 205.673,
          "en": "and that it should be refetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.673,
          "end": 209.67000000000002,
          "en": "And to achieve this, we should first of all go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "to the app JSX file where we create this Query client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "because it's with help of that Query client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 220.32,
          "en": "So with help of this object here, that we'll be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.32,
          "end": 224.34300000000002,
          "en": "to force this invalidation of a Query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.24,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "Therefore we should cut this from this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 234.05,
          "en": "and remove this import and instead add it to some other file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.47,
          "end": 239.31,
          "en": "from which we can then import it into multiple files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.31,
          "end": 243.93,
          "en": "In my case here, I'll just add it to this HTDP JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 248.49,
          "en": "There at the very top I'll export this Query client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.49,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "and of course for that we have to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 255.273,
          "en": "this Query client class that's being instantiated here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.06,
          "end": 262.02,
          "en": "Now with that exported here in HTDP JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.02,
          "end": 267.02,
          "en": "we should go back to App JSX and import this Query client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 274.79,
          "en": "from this HTDP JS file, which we find in the UTIL folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 276.57,
          "end": 279.78,
          "en": "Because we still need that Query client object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 279.78,
          "end": 282.453,
          "en": "to pass it to the Query client provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 283.53,
          "end": 286.621,
          "en": "But now we can use that same Query client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 286.621,
          "end": 290.953,
          "en": "in the new event JSX file here in On Success",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 290.953,
          "end": 295.02,
          "en": "because there, before navigating away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 295.02,
          "end": 297.78,
          "en": "I now want to use this Query client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 297.78,
          "end": 302.78,
          "en": "So we should import Query client from going up two levels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 304.35,
          "end": 309.35,
          "en": "and then UTIL and then HTDP JS and then in on success,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 312.09,
          "end": 315.75,
          "en": "so at a point of time where we know that it worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 315.75,
          "end": 320.75,
          "en": "I want to call Query client invalidate queries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 320.85,
          "end": 322.92,
          "en": "which does what its name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 322.92,
          "end": 327,
          "en": "It in the end tells React Query that the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 327,
          "end": 331.17,
          "en": "fetched by certain queries is outdated now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 331.17,
          "end": 332.4,
          "en": "that it should be marked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 337.35,
          "en": "as stale and that an immediate refetch should be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 337.35,
          "end": 339.81,
          "en": "if the Query belongs to a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 339.81,
          "end": 342.75,
          "en": "that's currently visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 342.75,
          "end": 344.97,
          "en": "So for example, if I'm creating a new event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 344.97,
          "end": 347.97,
          "en": "of course the page that shows all events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 347.97,
          "end": 350.01,
          "en": "is still visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 350.01,
          "end": 352.44,
          "en": "It's below this modal after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 352.44,
          "end": 354.63,
          "en": "So the Query that was responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 354.63,
          "end": 357.693,
          "en": "for this section here should be reexecuted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 359.76,
          "end": 363,
          "en": "And for that to target specific queries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 363,
          "end": 365.73,
          "en": "invalidate queries takes an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 365.73,
          "end": 369.57,
          "en": "as an input where we have to define the Query key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 369.57,
          "end": 370.833,
          "en": "which we wanna target.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 371.79,
          "end": 374.22,
          "en": "And this should of course be a Query key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 374.22,
          "end": 377.76,
          "en": "in the same format as we're using it for all those queries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 377.76,
          "end": 380.88,
          "en": "So an array which then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 380.88,
          "end": 382.803,
          "en": "could include the word events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 384.21,
          "end": 386.97,
          "en": "And this will then invalidate all queries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 386.97,
          "end": 389.46,
          "en": "that include this key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 389.46,
          "end": 393.15,
          "en": "It does not have to be exactly the same key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 393.15,
          "end": 395.956,
          "en": "So for example, in find events section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 395.956,
          "end": 399.09000000000003,
          "en": "I have a Query key that includes events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 399.09000000000003,
          "end": 402.87,
          "en": "and then also this object, this Query here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 402.87,
          "end": 405.93,
          "en": "with this key will also be invalidated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 405.93,
          "end": 408.42,
          "en": "because it includes events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.42,
          "end": 411.06,
          "en": "and I'm invalidating any Query key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 411.06,
          "end": 414.273,
          "en": "that does include events with that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 415.604,
          "end": 419.755,
          "en": "We could work around that by also setting the exact property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 419.755,
          "end": 422.22,
          "en": "on this object that we're passing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 422.22,
          "end": 426.72,
          "en": "to invalidate queries to true and now only queries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 426.72,
          "end": 430.202,
          "en": "with exactly that key would be invalidated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 430.202,
          "end": 433.35,
          "en": "But since you should build your Query keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 433.35,
          "end": 437.94,
          "en": "such that they kind of describe the data you are fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 437.94,
          "end": 442.74,
          "en": "it makes sense to invalidate all queries that include events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 442.74,
          "end": 444.48,
          "en": "because all those queries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 444.48,
          "end": 447.684,
          "en": "would otherwise be dealing with old data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 447.684,
          "end": 450.66,
          "en": "For example, here in find events section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 450.66,
          "end": 453.84000000000003,
          "en": "where I'm looking for events based on a search term",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 453.84000000000003,
          "end": 456.27,
          "en": "entered by the user, I of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 456.27,
          "end": 460.29,
          "en": "don't want to ignore new events that have been added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 460.29,
          "end": 463.62,
          "en": "So I wanna invalidate this Query as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 463.62,
          "end": 467.73,
          "en": "so that if a new event was added, that is met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 467.73,
          "end": 470.347,
          "en": "by this search term entered by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
